  "behavior": [
    "TRE compilation returns original syntax/allocation status through one cleanup path instead of terminating the host. Propagate previously ignored tag insertion, AST expansion, counting, transition metadata and initial-state metadata failures. Free clears the published TNFA and subgroup count before releasing storage, making cleanup idempotent and allowing error recovery to reuse a regex record.",
    "Private literal class identifiers and parameter addresses use distinct typed fields with safe accessors. Constructors initialize both; AST copy preserves both without integer-to-pointer encoding or exposed-provenance APIs.",
    "Tag insertion constructs every copied AST child field before publication, including num_submatches. Preserve copied subtree counts and reset transient tag/header state. This removes a genuine uninitialized read during bounded repeated-pattern expansion.",
    "Test-only thread-local allocator observation enumerates every allocation point for the selected production compile, rejects one allocation per run and records live allocations through cleanup. Hooks add no release failure configuration or quota changes.",
    "Public sub/gsub reject empty fixed patterns with GNU zero-length pattern error for ordinary/NA replacements and byte/character modes, including empty x. Fixed grep and empty ERE substitutions preserve valid behavior."
  ],
